What is Data Formatting in Data Analytics?

Data formatting is the process of changing data into a consistent, organized, and usable format so that it can be easily analyzed, visualized, or used in calculations.

Think of it as making messy data look and behave correctly.

Example

Suppose you have this data in Excel:

Name	Date	Salary	Gender
John	1/5/24	50000	M
Mary	05-01-2024	50,000	Female
Peter	January 5 2024	50000 KES	Male

The data represents similar information, but the formats are inconsistent.

You could format it as:

Name	Date	Salary	Gender
John	05/01/2024	50,000	Male
Mary	05/01/2024	50,000	Female
Peter	05/01/2024	50,000	Male

Now the data is consistent and easier to analyze.

