→ Convert them to the same unit if you're analyzing them together.

Formatting vs Cleaning

They are related but not exactly the same.

Data formatting = making the data's appearance and representation consistent.

Data cleaning = fixing errors, missing values, duplicates, incorrect entries, etc.

For example:

kenya, KENYA, Kenya

→ Formatting/standardization

Kenya, Keny, Kenya

→ Data cleaning because Keny is likely an incorrect value.

Simple definition to remember

Data formatting is organizing and standardizing the way data is represented so it can be easily read, analyzed, and interpreted.

For your Excel/data analytics learning, dates, numbers, currency, percentages, text, decimals, and units are the main formatting areas to understand.

